course: dictionary
lesson: 5055
title: Words carved and written
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An inscription is words that have been cut, carved or written on something so they will last. Stone, metal and coins are hard, so the words on them can stay for hundreds of years.
explain: «The Indus people used seals with short inscriptions and animal pictures, but nobody has yet worked out their writing.» The clues are seals and pictures: the words were put on small seals, and they are short. The sentence also says nobody can yet read them, so the inscriptions are words we still cannot understand.
explain: An inscription can also be handwritten words inside a book or on a photo, often to the person it is given to. Ask yourself: what is written, and where is it? If it is a message on a gift, it is an inscription.
fact: An inscription is words cut, carved or written on something hard, like stone, metal or a coin.
fact: Historians read inscriptions on old stones, monuments and coins to learn about the past.
fact: An inscription can also be handwritten words inside a book or on a photo, often to the person it is given to.
fact: «The Indus people used seals with short inscriptions and animal pictures.» We have not yet worked out what their writing says.
fact: Useful phrases: an inscription on, a short inscription, read the inscription.
exercise: «The Indus people used seals with short inscriptions and animal pictures.» What is an inscription in this sentence? | A kind of animal | A type of boat | *Words carved or cut on a seal | A picture of a river
exercise: Mum wrote an inscription inside my birthday book. What is an inscription here? | A torn page | *Words written by hand inside the book | A bookmark | A lock on the cover
exercise: Which word completes the phrase: read the ___ on the old stone? | *inscription | shadow | ticket | picture
test: «The trophy had an inscription with the winner's name.» What does inscription mean? | A list of rules | A cup for drinks | A winner's medal | *Words cut or engraved on the trophy
test: «She read the inscription inside the ring: To Anna, love Gran.» Why is there an inscription in the ring? | Rings must always have numbers | The ring is broken and needs words to fix it | *It names the person it is for and gives a short message | The metal is too shiny
exam: «The coin had a faint inscription that nobody could read.» What is an inscription? | A picture drawn in paint | *Words carved on the coin | A bright light shining from the metal | A small hole made for a chain
